@NAME@
JewCal, a pixel-art Jewish calendar for the GeekMagic SmallTV Pro (ESP32, 4 MB flash)

!! FOR THE SMALLTV *PRO* (ESP32, touch pad on top) ONLY.
!! The SmallTV and SmallTV Ultra use other chips (ESP8266, stock firmware
!! "Ultra-V9.x"; some newer SmallTVs have an ESP32-C2). Do NOT upload these
!! files through their "Firmware update" web page: an ESP8266 unit would no
!! longer boot and would need a serial adapter. The espflash and esptool
!! commands below name the chip (--chip esp32), so they refuse other boards.
!! SmallTV Ultra owners: use jewcal-ultra-<version>.zip (`make ultra-zip`).

FILES (all for the SmallTV Pro)
  jewcal-pro-full.bin   Bootloader + partition table + app. Write at 0x0.
                        Use this for a first install. It also clears saved settings.
  jewcal-pro-app.bin    The app alone. Write at 0x10000 to update a device that
                        already runs JewCal; WiFi and city settings are kept.
  jewcal-pro.elf        Debug symbols: `espflash monitor --elf jewcal-pro.elf`
                        turns crash backtraces into file:line.
  SHA256SUMS            Checksums of the files above.
  flash.sh              Flashes with espflash or esptool, whichever is installed:
                          ./flash.sh            fresh install
                          ./flash.sh --update   update, keeps settings
                          ./flash.sh --backup   save the current firmware first

BACK UP THE CURRENT FIRMWARE FIRST (optional, lets you go back to stock)
  espflash read-flash --chip esp32 0 0x400000 smalltv-backup.bin

FLASH (connect the SmallTV with a USB *data* cable)
  espflash:  espflash write-bin --chip esp32 0x0 jewcal-pro-full.bin
  esptool:   esptool.py --chip esp32 write_flash 0x0 jewcal-pro-full.bin
  browser:   https://espressif.github.io/esptool-js/
             Connect and check that it reports an ESP32 (not ESP32-C2), then
             add jewcal-pro-full.bin at offset 0x0 and Program.
  update:    espflash write-bin --chip esp32 0x10000 jewcal-pro-app.bin

FIRST RUN
  1. The screen shows SETUP. From a phone, join the WiFi network JEWCAL-XXXX.
  2. Open the address shown on the screen, pick your network, enter its password.
  3. After it restarts, open http://jewcal.local/ (or the IP shown on the info
     screen) and choose your city. Done: no further setup is needed.

BOARD VARIANT
  If the backlight never dims at night, your board drives it from GPIO21:
  build with `make zip FEATURES=backlight-gpio21`.

Calendar data: Hebcal.com. Weather data: Open-Meteo.com. Both CC BY 4.0.
